          "title": "Casino Hungarian",
          "subtitle": "Royal Casino",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hungarian Casino is a Royal Casino variant played in Hungary. Features numerical values for picture cards (J=11, Q=12, K=13, A=1/14) with unique building and capturing rules. Differs from Anglo-American Casino in several key ways."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hungarian Casino is a variant of Royal Casino played in Hungary. It represents the Central European tradition of Casino games where picture cards have numerical values, differing from the Anglo-American version where picture cards can only capture matching pictures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-4 players, typically playing individually."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard 52-card pack. Card values: 2-10=face value, J=11, Q=12, K=13, A=1 or 14."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard deck, score sheet"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Standard Casino dealing: cards to players and to table layout."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
